<p>Heyo, it's <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yellowislol" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6284593); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6284593&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1603397441" alt="YellowISlol" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6284593)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yellowislol" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6284593); return false;">YellowISlol</a></span> from &quot;The Furretsidence&quot;, and ima be dropping a crit today!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">The&nbsp;Crit!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;mean,&nbsp;what&nbsp;did&nbsp;you&nbsp;expect,&nbsp;legos?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Okay, let's start with what you did <em>right</em>: Well, your formatting on it was done really well. I can tell you were going for a sort of a theme that happens within a classroom. I also enjoyed the different fonts, it helped break it down for the eyes, as well as add <em>depth</em>. The colors had the same effect.</p>
<p>Now, let's look at what needs <em>improvement</em>: I mean, theres nothing that invokes humor in me. It's just a bunch of one-offs that would likely take place within a class. I didn't find myself enjoying this read, as it didn't have any <em>laugh effect</em>. Beyond that, the little extra things in the corner only made my eyes feel off. I feel like this would be better if there was something that was humorous at all. Add something relatable, that will make others laugh.</p>
<p>Beyond that, a joke article still needs to be related to the foundation. A note at the top or the bottom would help. Specifically, a note from the foundation about the object. A good example of what I mean can be found on the tale <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/sunfire|">Sunfire</a> (scroll to the bottom of the tale). However, I am not versed in canons at all, and if thats specifically because of the canon, you may ignore this line.</p>
<p>Finally, let's look at what simply <em>needs change</em>: Well, the light blue font is hardly visible here. You can hardly see it. The really cursive font on the third line of cursive doesn't show well, maybe use a different font of cursive for some readers.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyways, hope this is helpful!</p>
<p>~Yellow</p>

